DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The rriinntt(), rriinnttff(), and rriinnttll() functions return the integral value
     nearest to _x according to the prevailing rounding mode.  These functions
     raise an inexact exception when the original argument is not an exact in‐
     teger.

     The nneeaarrbbyyiinntt(), nneeaarrbbyyiinnttff(), and nneeaarrbbyyiinnttll() functions perform the
     same operation, except that they do not raise an inexact exception.

